# PocketClaw production signing certificate — SHA-256 fingerprint.
#
# PUBLIC METADATA. This file holds one thing: the SHA-256 digest of the
# production signing *certificate*. A certificate is the public half. It is not
# a key, it carries no password, and publishing it is normal — Google Play shows
# it, and anyone can read it out of a signed APK with apksigner. Committing it
# is the point: it is what lets the release gate prove that an artifact was
# signed by the key this project intends to ship with, and not by some other key
# that also happens to verify.
#
# NEVER put the keystore, an alias password, or any key material in this file or
# anywhere else in this repository. See docs/RELEASE_SIGNING.md.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS: NOT ENROLLED
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No production signing key has been created yet, so there is deliberately no
# digest below. This is not an oversight and it must not be "filled in to make
# the gate pass": until a real key exists, production artifact verification is
# supposed to fail, and it reports this file's absence of an enrolled signer as
# the reason.
#
# A placeholder digest here would be worse than nothing. It would either fail
# against every real artifact for a confusing reason, or — if someone chose a
# value that matched something — quietly certify the wrong key.
#
# To enroll after the key ceremony (H2), add exactly one line below containing
# the 64-character lowercase hex digest and nothing else:
#
#     0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
#
# Read it from the keystore you just created with:
#
#     keytool -list -v -keystore <keystore> -alias <alias> \
#       | grep -A1 'SHA256:' 
#
# or from a signed artifact with:
#
#     apksigner verify --print-certs <apk> | grep 'SHA-256 digest'
#
# keytool prints it colon-separated and uppercase; this file wants it lowercase
# with the colons removed.
